  "about": {"title": "Box braids, free ends", "category": "Braids", "description": "Box braids that come undone below a hair tie: with end free the hair leaves its sections past the weave (over release braid widths) and runs on along the braid's path as one plain bundle, which the nodes after the Braid style. The Braid writes braidTail per point (0 in the braid, 1 in the free tail): the Clump's strength and the Curl's radius mapped by it gather and curl the ends alone."},
